{title: Faithful Mother of Levi}
{subtitle: Exodus 6:20; Numbers 26:59; Exodus 2:1–2; Hebrews 11:23; Exodus 2:3–4; 2:5–9}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Gm7] | [Eb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
A daughter of [Bb]Levi in Egypt lived [Gm]
Amram married [Eb]her, the covenant kept [F]
She bore [Bb]Aaron and Miriam too
Moses came [Gm]when the decree stood
The king com[Eb]manded to kill the boys
[F]But she saw the beauty of the child's [Bb]face
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Pre-Chorus}
She [Eb]hid him for three full months
Not afraid [Gm]of the king's heavy command
[Eb]Faith stood strong in the land
When she could [F]hide him no longer
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
She made a [Bb]basket of papyrus
[Gm]Coated with tar and pitch
[Eb]Laid the child in it gently
[F]Set it among the reeds on the [Bb]Nile
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
His sister stood at a distance
Watching to [Gm]see what would be
Pharaoh's [Eb]daughter came to the river
To [F]bathe by the water's edge
She saw the bas[Gm]ket in the reeds
Sent her slave [Eb]girl to fetch it
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
She [Eb]opened it and saw the boy
Cry[Gm]ing, a baby boy
She felt [Eb]sorry for him
Said this is [F]one of the Hebrew children
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
His sis[Bb]ter asked to find a nurse
A He[Gm]brew woman to help
Pharao[Eb]h's daughter agreed and said
[F]Go, find her and bring her here
Joche[Gm]bed came and took the child
Nursed [Eb]him for wages paid
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
By [Eb]faith his parents hid him
Not afraid [Gm]of the king's edict
A [Eb]faithful mother of Levi
[F]Saw the beauty of God's [Bb]plan
{end_of_verse}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
| [Bb] | [Gm7] | [Eb] | [F] |
